endobj
1815 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Chemical recycling technologies are generally optimized for specific polymer types such as polyolefins or polystyrene. In contrast, municipal waste streams tend to be mixed and inconsistent, often containing multilayer materials and trace contaminants. Navigating this variability is central to effective process design. Some technology providers have developed capabilities in segregating and pre-processing target plastics, improving feedstock quality and system reliability.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1816 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (2\) Product Quality and Purification)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [7]
>>
